---
title: Barbecue lamb shawarma
tags: [middle eastern, lamb, smoker, weekend, make-ahead]
cuisine: middle eastern
source: BBQ Lamb Shawarma by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/bbq-lamb-shawarma
---

> The lamb makes enough for many sandwiches; the assembly below is for one.

== Garlic marinade ==

Toast the @cumin seeds{1/2%tsp}, @coriander seeds{1/2%tsp}, @ground Aleppo pepper{1/2%tsp} and @fennel seeds{1/4%tsp} in a dry #sauté pan{} over medium heat until they smell toasty. Cool, then grind fine in a #mortar and pestle{} and tip out.

Pound the @garlic{6%cloves}(peeled), @ginger{2%tbsp}(chopped) and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} to a smooth paste in the mortar.

Move the paste to a small bowl and stir in the ground spices, @blended oil{1/4%cup} and @dried oregano{1/4%tsp} until it comes together. Keep in the fridge.

== Pulled lamb ==

Heat a #smoker{} to 250°F.

Rub the @lamb shoulder{5%lb}(rinsed and patted dry) with 2 oz of the garlic marinade and season it well with @kosher salt{}. Leave at room temperature ~{1%hour}.

Smoke fat side up ~{3%hours}, turning it now and then so the bark forms evenly.

Drop the smoker to 200°F and smoke ~{4%hours} more, until the bark is dark but not dry. Spritz with @apple cider vinegar{}.

Raise the smoker to 275°F, wrap the lamb in butcher paper and smoke ~{2%hours} more, until the meat reads 200°F inside.

Rest the wrapped lamb ~{2%hours} in a warm, insulated box. Shred it, discarding bones and sinew, and refrigerate.

== Tahini sauce ==

Whisk the @tahini{1/2%cup}, @garlic{1%clove}(grated), the juice of @lemon{1/2} and @water{2%tbsp}(ice-cold) until pale and fluffy.

== Tomato and cucumber salad ==

Toss the @tomato{1}(cut in wedges), @Persian cucumber{1}(seeded, quartered), @red onion{1/4}(thinly sliced), @parsley{4%sprigs}(chopped) and @mint{2%sprigs}(chopped). Season with the juice of @lemon{1} and @kosher salt{}.

== Assembly ==

Warm the @laffa{1} on a #griddle{} until soft, and keep the griddle hot.

Heat a little @blended oil{} in a #cast-iron skillet{} over medium heat. Crisp 5 oz of the pulled lamb ~{4%minutes}, until hot through.

Toss the lamb with the juice of @lemon{1/2}, a few chopped herbs and the @pickled cherry peppers{2%oz}.

Cut a pocket in the laffa and spread the inside with the @hummus{4%oz}. Fill with the salad, the lamb and the @potatoes{4%oz}(roasted until crisp), and drizzle with tahini sauce.

Fold in the sides and roll it up tightly. Sear seam side down on the griddle until crisp and sealed, then turn and crisp the other side. Serve hot.
